# Phase 18 Common MessageUtils parity follow-up — 2026-10-16T08:50Z

- Baseline revision: `12db9def`; pinned Java 5.5.1 source commit:
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.
- P18-V01 source review found the four public Common `MessageUtils` methods
  missing from Rust: the Murmur3-32 sharding index helper, message and
  collection adapters, and encoded-property deletion. Added the Rust mappings,
  a pure Guava-compatible Murmur3-32 implementation, Java invoked fixture
  generation/verification, a Rust differential test, and Phase 8 / P18 audit
  documentation. Fixture SHA-256:
  `e01bed78a2a2290a82991fd68d308d77c283475e82b32d32d3939d045099f5f8`.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --locked` passed, including the new
  fixture differential. Full `cargo test --workspace --locked` and
  `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked` passed. Strict
  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D
  warnings`, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `git diff --check` passed.
- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` passed all 37 scenarios,
  fixture checks, Java probes and cross-decodes; the new MessageUtils fixture
  was verified. Differential self-test and 37-scenario manifest validation
  passed.
- `bash tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh` passed 16 cases × 3 repetitions.
  The bounded fuzz smoke passed with 105 frame seeds, 11 message seeds and
  1,856 mutations. Release examples and the offline benchmark compiled. The
  Asia/Taipei Unique ID fixture passed.
- Workspace metadata/license/dependency checks passed. All seven
  `cargo package --list --locked --allow-dirty` listings contained `LICENSE`
  and `NOTICE`; `--allow-dirty` was needed because the new Common sources were
  not committed yet.
- During setup, direct Maven main-class override selected the configured
  `compat.Main`; the fixture was then generated through its new
  `message-utils-fixture` dispatch and Maven verification passed. The first
  Common integration build used the wrong public path for
  `PROPERTY_SHARDING_KEY`; corrected it to `message::constants` and the scoped
  plus workspace tests passed. Neither issue was a product failure.
- This closes only the surfaced `MessageUtils` declaration and behavior slice.
  The broad bidirectional P18-V01 audit remains open. Current-revision GitHub
  Ubuntu/P18-V04 evidence is still absent; Phase 19 Docker/Broker execution,
  owner deployment validation, and release preflight remain later work.
- No plan files changed. No Docker, Broker, push, tag, publication,
  deployment, or compatibility claim was made.

P18-V01 Common CorrelationIdUtil API slice (2026-10-16)

- Pinned Java client 5.5.1 source commit
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` declares public static
  `CorrelationIdUtil.createCorrelationId()` returning
  `UUID.randomUUID().toString()`. Common now exposes
  `rocketmq_classic_common::utils::create_correlation_id`; Producer request
  preparation uses that function, and the duplicate Producer-only
  implementation/direct `rand` dependency are removed. Common now owns the
  existing `rand` dependency.
- `RequestReplyFixtures` inventories the Java method signature in
  `fixtures/producer/request-reply.json`; Rust checks the inventory and UUID v4
  lowercase 8-4-4-4-12 format. Fixture SHA-256:
  `295307a1f559b7afa30179b48a83b0ac008716a8a1b421872b440c6ff097153c`.
- The new Rust API test first failed because Common had no public `utils`
  module, then passed after implementation. One initial Maven fixture-generation
  invocation ran from the workspace root and wrote its relative output outside
  the repo; that generated file was removed, and fixture generation was rerun
  successfully from `compat/java-reference`. No unintended external artifact
  remains.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --locked` passed (23 unit tests, all
  integration and doc tests). `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked`
  passed (142 unit tests and all integration/doc targets). Strict all-target,
  all-feature Clippy passed for Common and Producer. `mvn -f
  compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` passed, including the 37-scenario
  manifest, fixture drift checks and Java/Rust cross-decodes. Workspace format
  and diff checks passed.
- Updated the Phase 8/15 crosswalks, Phase 6 API map/audit, release checklist,
  and this append-only log. No plan changed. This closes only this Common API
  slice; broad bidirectional P18-V01 remains open. Full workspace P18-V02 must
  be rerun after the remaining code audit. No Docker/Broker, push, tag,
  publication, deployment or compatibility claim was made.
